            }
          ],
          "message": {
            "text": "Debug mode is explicitly enabled in server code or configuration. Depending on the framework and deployment, error details or a debugger may become externally accessible. Remediation: Disable debug mode in deployed services and return sanitized errors while retaining protected server-side diagnostics. Agent/MCP relevance: An agent API or MCP server may handle secrets, prompts and privileged tools. A reachable development debugger or verbose exception page can reveal that state and, in some frameworks, permit code execution. Fix steps: 1. Set the production server/framework debug option to false, remove development-server launch flags, and use the supported production server configuration. Verify: Start the deployed configuration in staging and trigger a controlled exception; verify there is no interactive debugger or detailed client traceback. 2. Return a minimal error identifier and safe message. Keep detailed server diagnostics in access-controlled logs with credential/prompt redaction. Verify: Use a synthetic secret marker in a failing request and confirm it is absent from the HTTP/MCP error and unauthorized log views. 3. Remove debug overrides from environment files, image defaults and orchestration manifests; require an explicit separate development profile. Verify: Inspect effective deployment settings and validate the production startup fails or alerts if the development profile is selected."
          },
          "partialFingerprints": {
            "agentMcpScan/v1": "8f8e715e8f65d28379ca9bd4"
